<tool id="zenodo_download_unzip" name="Zenodo download and unzip" version="@DOWNLOAD_VERSION@+galaxy@DOWNLOAD_SUFFIX@" profile="@PROFILE@">
    <description>for a work list, with a manifest of every file</description>
    <macros>
        <import>macros.xml</import>
    </macros>
    <expand macro="requirements_download"/>
    <required_files>
        <include path="zenodo_download_unzip.py"/>
    </required_files>
    <version_command>echo @DOWNLOAD_VERSION@</version_command>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
        #import re
        mkdir -p prefetched &&
        #if $prefetched:
            #for $file in $prefetched:
                ## Same naming rule as safe_name() in the script.
                ln -s '$file' 'prefetched/${re.sub(r"[^\w.\-]", "_", str($file.element_identifier))}' &&
            #end for
        #end if
        python '$__tool_directory__/zenodo_download_unzip.py'
        '$work_list'
        --prefetched-dir prefetched
        --work-dir work
        --raw-dir raw_files
        --bundle-dir context_bundles
        --context-dir context_files
        --manifest '$manifest'
        --tool-version '@DOWNLOAD_VERSION@+galaxy@DOWNLOAD_SUFFIX@'
        #if str($pipeline_version).strip():
            --pipeline-version '$pipeline_version'
        #end if
    ]]></command>
    <inputs>
        <param name="work_list" type="data" format="json" label="Work list (work_list.json)" help="Written by the NOMAD side: the records and files to download, the limits and the extension lists."/>
        <param name="prefetched" type="data_collection" collection_type="list" optional="true" label="Files already in Galaxy" help="Optional list. An element whose identifier is exactly a Zenodo file key is used instead of downloading that file, for example a file imported through Galaxy's Zenodo file source. Its MD5 is still checked."/>
        <param name="pipeline_version" type="text" value="" optional="true" label="Pipeline version for the manifest" help="Written as tool_version into the manifest. The NOMAD side retries failed files when it changes, so the workflow sets it to the converter's version. Left empty, this tool's version is used.">
            <validator type="regex" message="Letters, digits, spaces and . _ + - only">^[\w .+\-]*$</validator>
        </param>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="manifest" format="json" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Manifest"/>
        <collection name="raw_files" type="list" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Raw files">
            <discover_datasets pattern="__designation__" directory="raw_files" format="binary" sort_by="filename"/>
        </collection>
        <collection name="context_bundles" type="list" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Context bundles">
            <discover_datasets pattern="__designation__" directory="context_bundles" format="json" sort_by="filename"/>
        </collection>
        <collection name="context_files" type="list" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Context files">
            <discover_datasets pattern="__designation__" directory="context_files" format="binary" sort_by="filename"/>
        </collection>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <!-- Test 01: archive with raw, context, junk and known files; unsafe, too large and mismatching files. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="4">
            <param name="work_list" value="work_list.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="prefetched">
                <collection type="list">
                    <element name="stm_archive.zip" value="stm_archive.zip" ftype="zip"/>
                    <element name="traversal.zip" value="traversal.zip" ftype="zip"/>
                    <element name="loose_readme.rtf" value="loose_readme.rtf" ftype="txt"/>
                    <element name="loose_raw.sxm" value="loose_raw.sxm" ftype="binary"/>
                    <element name="loose_mismatch.txt" value="loose_mismatch.txt" ftype="txt"/>
                </collection>
            </param>
            <param name="pipeline_version" value="pynxtools_dataconverter 0.4.1+galaxy0"/>
            <output name="manifest" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="&quot;run_id&quot;: &quot;test-batch-001&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;tool_version&quot;: &quot;pynxtools_dataconverter 0.4.1+galaxy0&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;status&quot;: &quot;extracted&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;reason&quot;: &quot;unsafe_path&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;reason&quot;: &quot;too_large&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;reason&quot;: &quot;md5_mismatch&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;reason&quot;: &quot;unsupported_archive&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;action&quot;: &quot;already_known&quot;" n="2"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;role&quot;: &quot;ignored&quot;" n="5"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;STM data/session 1/notes.md&quot;"/>
                    <not_has_text text="evil.txt"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <!-- Elements are sorted by file name. -->
            <output_collection name="raw_files" type="list" count="3">
                <element name="17533355-0d16b332fc2e-loose_raw.sxm" ftype="binary"/>
                <element name="17533355-bde42f7aaf67-const_dos_No14_003.sxm" ftype="binary">
                    <assert_contents>
                        <has_size value="113993"/>
                    </assert_contents>
                </element>
                <element name="17533355-c941e1bfe103-broken.sxm" ftype="binary"/>
            </output_collection>
            <output_collection name="context_bundles" type="list" count="3">
                <element name="17533355-bde42f7aaf67-const_dos_No14_003.sxm" ftype="json">
                    <assert_contents>
                        <has_text text="Sample: magnetic adatom chains on a superconductor"/>
                        <has_text text="Tip: W"/>
                        <has_text text="Instrument: Nanonis SPM, low temperature"/>
                        <not_has_text text="fonttbl"/>
                    </assert_contents>
                </element>
            </output_collection>
            <!-- 3 context files, plus image.png and nested.zip: all non-raw files no ignore pattern matches. -->
            <output_collection name="context_files" type="list" count="5"/>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 02: the zip's index is above the uncompressed limit, so nothing is extracted. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="4">
            <param name="work_list" value="work_list_uncompressed_limit.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="prefetched">
                <collection type="list">
                    <element name="stm_archive.zip" value="stm_archive.zip" ftype="zip"/>
                </collection>
            </param>
            <output name="manifest" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="&quot;reason&quot;: &quot;uncompressed_limit&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;files&quot;: []"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;tool_version&quot;: &quot;@DOWNLOAD_VERSION@+galaxy@DOWNLOAD_SUFFIX@&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output_collection name="raw_files" type="list" count="0"/>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 03: a work list without records gives an empty manifest and empty collections. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="4">
            <param name="work_list" value="work_list_empty.json" ftype="json"/>
            <output name="manifest" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="&quot;archives&quot;: []"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;files&quot;: []"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output_collection name="raw_files" type="list" count="0"/>
            <output_collection name="context_bundles" type="list" count="0"/>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 04: context files keep a fixed type, also when Galaxy cannot detect it (binary
             bytes in a .csv). A detected type "auto" would stop the report step from scheduling. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="4">
            <param name="work_list" value="work_list_loose.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="prefetched">
                <collection type="list">
                    <element name="loose_readme.rtf" value="loose_readme.rtf" ftype="txt"/>
                    <element name="loose_raw.sxm" value="loose_raw.sxm" ftype="binary"/>
                    <element name="context_unknown.csv" value="context_unknown.csv" ftype="binary"/>
                </collection>
            </param>
            <output_collection name="raw_files" type="list" count="1">
                <element name="17533355-0d16b332fc2e-loose_raw.sxm" ftype="binary"/>
            </output_collection>
            <output_collection name="context_files" type="list" count="2">
                <element name="17533355-110009dcee21-context_unknown.csv" ftype="binary">
                    <assert_contents>
                        <has_size value="512"/>
                    </assert_contents>
                </element>
                <element name="17533355-d6dd8682843d-loose_readme.rtf" ftype="binary"/>
            </output_collection>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 05: PDF text goes into the bundle as pdf_text. A broken PDF and a PDF without a
             text layer are only reported in the bundle; their files are still kept. context_sm_page2.pdf: page 2 of the Supplementary
             Material of Zenodo record 17202182 (CC-BY-4.0). -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="4">
            <param name="work_list" value="work_list_pdf.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="prefetched">
                <collection type="list">
                    <element name="loose_raw.sxm" value="loose_raw.sxm" ftype="binary"/>
                    <element name="context_sm_page2.pdf" value="context_sm_page2.pdf" ftype="pdf"/>
                    <element name="context_broken.pdf" value="context_broken.pdf" ftype="binary"/>
                    <element name="context_no_text.pdf" value="context_no_text.pdf" ftype="pdf"/>
                </collection>
            </param>
            <output name="manifest" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="&quot;role&quot;: &quot;context&quot;" n="3"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;files&quot;: ["/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;download_failures&quot;: []"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output_collection name="context_bundles" type="list" count="1">
                <element name="17533355-0d16b332fc2e-loose_raw.sxm" ftype="json">
                    <assert_contents>
                        <!-- Two-column text in reading order, as in the tested LLM context. -->
                        <has_text text="low-temperature scanning tunneling microscope (JT-SPECS GmbH)"/>
                        <has_text text="The crystals were cleaved at approximately 100 K"/>
                        <has_text text="&quot;pdf_text_error&quot;: &quot;unreadable&quot;"/>
                        <has_text text="&quot;pdf_text_error&quot;: &quot;no_text&quot;"/>
                        <has_text text="&quot;pdf_text_error&quot;: null"/>
                        <has_text text="&quot;text&quot;: null" n="3"/>
                        <!-- The work list's user, for the ELN. -->
                        <has_text text="&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Test Person&quot;"/>
                    </assert_contents>
                </element>
            </output_collection>
            <output_collection name="context_files" type="list" count="3"/>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
**What it does**

Downloads the files of a **work list** from [Zenodo](https://zenodo.org) with
[zenodo_get](https://github.com/dvolgyes/zenodo_get), checks each file's MD5 against the
work list, extracts `.zip` archives safely and classifies every file. It is the first step of
the Zenodo → Galaxy → NOMAD harvest; the work list comes from the NOMAD side
([nomad-eosc-galaxy-actions](https://github.com/FAIRmat-NFDI/nomad-eosc-galaxy-actions)).

-----

**Safe extraction**

An archive is refused, and nothing of it extracted, when a member path is absolute, contains
`..` or is a symbolic link ("zip slip"), or when its total uncompressed size is above the work
list's limit ("zip bomb"). Archives inside an archive are not extracted.

-----

**Classification**

- `raw`: extension in `raw_extensions`. Converted once per record, unless its SHA-256 is in the
  record's `known_sha256`.
- `context`: extension in `context_extensions`, for example a readme. A raw file's context is the
  context files in its own folder and every parent folder of the same archive, plus the record's
  loose context files.
- `ignored`: matches `ignore_patterns`, or has neither extension.

-----

**Outputs**

- **Manifest**: one row per archive and per file, with SHA-256, role, action and reason.
  Downloads that failed for loose files are listed under `download_failures`.
- **Raw files**: the raw files to convert.
- **Context bundles**: one JSON per raw file, with the same element identifier, holding the
  record metadata and the text of the raw file's context files. The text of a PDF is read with
  [pdftotext](https://poppler.freedesktop.org/) into `pdf_text`; a PDF without text (broken,
  scanned, too large) gets the reason in `pdf_text_error` and the run goes on.
- **Context files**: the record's context files, for the NOMAD project.

Element identifiers are `<record ID>-<first 12 characters of the SHA-256>-<file name>`.
    ]]></help>
    <citations>
        <expand macro="citation_zenodo_get"/>
    </citations>
    <expand macro="creators"/>
</tool>
